  "articleBody": "While some home projects are great for a DIY weekend, window casing can throw some curveballs that really warrant a professional touch. So, when should you pick up the phone? First, if your window isn't perfectly square, plumb, or level, that’s a big red flag. Trying to force trim onto an uneven opening will just highlight the imperfections. A pro knows how to shim and adjust to make it look right. Second, if your walls are uneven, getting that crisp, tight joint between the casing and the wall becomes incredibly difficult; an expert can assess and prep the surface properly. Third, custom trim profiles or needing to match existing historical trim can be incredibly challenging. It requires specific tools, skills, and an eye for detail to replicate or seamlessly blend new with old. Finally, if you want a really flawless, high-end look where every miter joint is tight, every reveal is consistent, and the finish is impeccable, that’s when a qualified professional really shines. Businesses like HH Remodeling LLC specialize in finish carpentry and can ensure your window casings are installed with precision and care, saving you headaches and rework down the line.",
